Z||000000||86SE||03-17-2000||12:19 AM||||Wednesday morning I drove my 86 Fiero V-6 to school and drove for about 9 miles at 65 MPH (gas was one notch before E)  i pulled into the gas station because I was about running on fumes, filled it half full.  Then drove it 3 blocks to school, then stopped at a stop sign and just started to pull away then the engine started to die but tried to keep going but stalled.  I coasted to a parking spot and tried to restart it.  After about 15-20 seconds on the starter I decided it was not going to start.<P>At lunch break I went out to see if she would fire up, sure enough it did!!  Then I started driving back home (drove 4 miles) then the engine jerked hard just once when I was passing a pickup but dident stall, but very close to.<P>Could this be a partialy clogged fuel filter??  I dont want it to die on me when I half way to school!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000001||Oreif||03-17-2000||02:17 AM||||Do you remember if there was a gas truck at the gas station? If you fill up your tank while the truck fills the gound tanks you could have lots-o-dirt. The filling of the ground tanks stirs up lot of sediment. Changing the fuel filter should help. <BR>The only other thing I've seen cause simular problems was water in the gas. Try putting in some "Heet" or another brand of gasline antifreeze/cleaner. This should remove the water.||||reg||1
